      "observed": "The isolated CAN transceivers U10 and U11 have both GND1 and GND2 pins connected to the same system GND net.",
      "expected": "For the intended isolated CAN buses, GND1 and GND2 of each isolated CAN transceiver should be separate ground domains, not tied together.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "U10.4(GND1,power_in) U10.5(GND2,power_in) U11.4(GND1,power_in) U11.5(GND2,power_in)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses ... through an isolated CAN transceiver"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "This defeats the galvanic isolation of the CAN interfaces and can introduce ground loops or noise coupling between the logic side and the CAN side.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": [
        "D30",
        "R60"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "D30.2",
        "D30.4",
        "R60.1",
        "R60.2"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "ESTOP_OUT",
        "Net-(D30-K2)"
      ],
      "observed": "The second LED element of D30 has its anode pin D30.4 connected directly to ESTOP_OUT, while its cathode pin D30.2 is connected through R60 to the same ESTOP_OUT net.",
      "expected": "An indicator LED should have its anode tied to a supply or LED-power net and its cathode driven by the status signal through a current-limit resistor, as done for D30.3/D30.1 and the other LEDs on /LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "ESTOP_OUT : D30.4(A2,input) J13.6(Pin_6,passive) J2.6(Pin_6,passive) R60.2(passive) U36.4(Y,output)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(D30-K2) : D30.2(K2,input) R60.1(passive)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The second element of D30 cannot light because both terminals are held at the same potential, so the intended ESTOP indicator function is lost.",
      "confidence": 0.65
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build contains at least two deviations: the isolated CAN transceiver grounds are shorted to common GND, defeating the intended CAN isolation, and one LED element of D30 is effectively shorted across itself on ESTOP_OUT."
}

